Week 03 — System Resources, File Systems & Access Control

This week focused on understanding how an operating system manages system resources, files, directories, users, groups, permissions, and access control.

These concepts are important cybersecurity foundations because they help explain how systems control access to resources and how incorrect permissions or excessive privileges can create security risks.

