Basic Permission Model

Read    → View / read data
Write   → Modify data
Execute → Run a file or access a directory appropriately

Security Connection

Incorrect permissions can allow users or processes to access resources they should not be able to access.

The Principle of Least Privilege means giving users and processes only the permissions they actually need.

